    The cost the note warned about is `charsNear`, and it is affordable: a flight is
    four to seven bodies against a world that boots with six hundred and thirty-three.
    `spawnEyeFlight` puts them up sharing one squad.
    THE INVERSION IS THE CREATURE. They are named for the warding light — the small
    terrible sun their own kin will not close on — and they turn it on you. Each one is
    0.42x across with 22 blood and a claw of 3; the threat is the GAZE, which is
    `emberrot`, a rot-fire on a timer rather than a blow that lands.
    AND THAT IS THE BALANCE LEVER THE NOTE ASKED FOR, and it needed no new code at all:
    `applyDot` already passes `raw` to applyDamage with the comment "a fire already
    burning on the skin is past the plate". Measured on two identical bodies, one in
    plate and one bare: 43 points of wound against 45. The armour bought nothing. That
    is the intended counter to a host whose survivability comes out of `def`.
    Spawned at tide 2 and up, and rare inside it — armour-blind is the right thing to
    meet late and the wrong thing to meet in week one.

