    wants a BIGGER budget; lines PAINTED into the albedo get reproduced more faithfully
    by a bigger budget and get worse. Luminance spread across the baked vertex colours,
    which is what a flat-shaded model actually shows: Lyonart 27.8, Lyre v2 45.4, and
    the head v2 replaced 38.9. Painted — and v2 was more contrasty than the one the
    owner had already called "a bit off".
    THE OBVIOUS NUMBER WAS THE WRONG NUMBER, and a sweep against it wasted an hour
    before that was clear. Six smoothing passes moved global sdev 45.4 -> 36.7 and then
    plateaued, still miles from Lyonart's 27.8, because most of Lyre's spread is her
    near-white hair against her skin — legitimate LARGE-scale contrast that has to stay,
    and flattening toward it would leave a pasty oval. A painted wrinkle is precisely a
    vertex sitting far from the ones touching it, so measure that instead:
        lyonart  fine detail mean 6.05    lyre v2  16.08   (2.7x)
    Against that metric the pass responds properly — 2x/0.5 gives 10.81, 4x/0.35 gives
    7.75, 5x/0.3 gives 6.78. Shipped at 5x/0.3: 1.12x Lyonart, from 2.66x.
    SO IT IS UNSHARP MASKING RUN BACKWARDS. A few Laplacian passes over the colour give
    the low-frequency field; the high-frequency remainder is scaled to 0.3 and added
    back. The mesh is untouched — same 2,004 verts, same positions, byte-identical `p`
    stream, only `c` changed.
    THE IRISES ARE FROZEN, AND SO IS THE RING AROUND THEM. "Keeping the red eyes intact"
    is the half of the request that a heavier pass would quietly delete: 38 of 2,004
    vertices carry chroma over 40/255 and every one is an iris — two per cent of the
    mesh, so bleeding them into the skin would cost nothing anything else could notice.
    Saturated verts are locked, and their immediate neighbours too, or the iris ends up
    with a pink halo where skin averaged into it. 33 red vertices before, 33 after.
    AND A NEGATIVE CONTROL SAYS WHERE THE FLOOR IS. Baked again at HEAD_DETAIL=0 — every
    trace of painted detail gone — and rendered beside the shipped 0.3: near enough
    identical. What is left around her mouth and brow is the SCULPT'S OWN GEOMETRY, not
    paint, so there is nothing further to win by smoothing colour harder. 0.3 is the
    landing spot, not a compromise on the way to a better one.
    THE ASSERTION IS A RATIO, because the request was comparative. lyre and czarina go
    through a 1.6x-Lyonart gate; Saga is exempted BY NAME (a hollow with a deliberately
    blotched hide, 1.82x) rather than by widening the bound until it catches nothing.
    Run against the pre-fix build it prints "PAINTED LINES ARE BACK — lyre at 2.66x".
    ONE RECORD SPLICED, NOT A TABLE REGENERATED — same reason as the bake before it: the
    other three source .glb files are not in this repo and a full run would silently
    delete them.

